---
import {recognitionDocuments,qualificationEmail} from '../data/aboutEditorial';
const documents=[recognitionDocuments[1],recognitionDocuments[2],recognitionDocuments[0]];
---
<section class="al-section al-credentials" id="documents" aria-labelledby="al-credentials-heading">
 <header class="al-section-head"><h2 id="al-credentials-heading">Company recognition<br/>&amp; supplier documents</h2><p>Review the original enterprise recognition and teaching partnership documents. These records serve different purposes from the ISO 9001 quality-system certificate.</p></header>
 <div class="al-credential-grid" id="al-original-documents">
  {documents.map(document=><article class="al-credential">
   <figure class="al-credential-image" data-image-origin="original-company-document"><a href={document.image} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label={'View original document: '+document.title}><img src={document.image} width={document.width} height={document.height} alt={document.title+', original Chinese document'} loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a></figure>
   <p class="al-kicker">{document.kind}</p><h3>{document.title}</h3>
   <details class="al-credential-details"><summary>Document details &amp; dates</summary><p>{document.description}</p><dl><div><dt>Printed date / validity</dt><dd>{document.date}</dd></div><div><dt>What it covers</dt><dd>{document.scope}</dd></div></dl></details>
   <a class="al-inline-link" href={document.image} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View original document<span class="sr-only">: {document.title}</span></a>
  </article>)}
 </div>
 <p class="al-small al-credential-note">Dates and validity describe the displayed originals. Request the current status when qualifying LZZ as a supplier.</p>
 <div class="al-certificate-request" id="quality-system"><div><h3>ISO 9001 quality-system certificate</h3><p>LZZ is ISO 9001 certified. Request the current certificate, holder, scope and validity for your supplier review.</p></div><a class="al-secondary" href={qualificationEmail}>Request current ISO 9001 certificate</a></div>
 <details class="al-order-records" id="al-order-records"><summary>Records to agree for your part</summary><div><p>Company qualification and order acceptance need different evidence. Define the records your purchasing and quality teams require.</p><ul><li>Material grade, condition and traceability records</li><li>Critical dimensions, datums and inspection report format</li><li>Sampling, final surface condition and acceptance criteria</li><li>Any project-specific standards or additional documentation</li></ul><a class="al-inline-link" href="/factory/#quality">Review inspection and documentation requirements</a></div></details>
</section>
